[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3700024223","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114355#issuecomment-3700024223","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114355","id":3700024223,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7cieOf","user":{"login":"goatchurchprime","id":677254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzI1NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/677254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime","html_url":"https://github.com/goatchurchprime","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-30T17:28:49Z","updated_at":"2025-12-30T17:28:49Z","body":"There is an official godot demo of the audio spectrum effect https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/audio/spectrum which is not good enough to show off this bad issue.  \r\n\r\nAs well as being good enough to show off bugs, I believe demo projects should also illustrate what the different parameters do.  So, for example, the demo could show 4 spectrum analyzers side by side with different `fft_size` values so you can visibly see the compromise between smoothness and latency.  Also, the sine sweep from the [original issue](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/67650#issue-1415650951) is _much_ better for explaining what an FFT does. \r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3700024223/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3700095429","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114355#issuecomment-3700095429","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114355","id":3700095429,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7civnF","user":{"login":"Akosmo","id":95504962,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbFKQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95504962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo","html_url":"https://github.com/Akosmo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-30T18:05:59Z","updated_at":"2025-12-30T18:12:18Z","body":"Tested with the project provided in the [original issue](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/67650). It's indeed fixed on my end. Other people in the issue page also confirmed that removing the while loop fixed the issue for them.\r\n\r\nWould be great to reviews on this. It's kind of a niche part of the engine, but it's also just broken, it seems.\r\nI was initially worried that removing code that dealt with time of FFT capture would break something, but the only thing it was used for was that while loop.\r\nThere's the idea of having a \"legacy\" mode for this, but I personally don't think it's necessary. Not only it seems these changes don't break anything (need reviews), but the current version on stable is already broken.\r\n\r\nAlso, I agree with @goatchurchprime . We could use a demo project that demonstrates the spectrum analyzer better.\r\n\r\nEdit: issue still happens on 4.5.1, by the way.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3700095429/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3708720251","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114355#issuecomment-3708720251","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114355","id":3708720251,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dDpR7","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T02:18:33Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T02:18:33Z","body":"> Also, the sine sweep from the https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/67650#issue-1415650951 is much better for explaining what an FFT does.\r\n\r\nWhat's the difference between the current demo and a sine sweep? (I'm not an audio specialist.)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3708720251/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3708757274","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114355#issuecomment-3708757274","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114355","id":3708757274,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dDyUa","user":{"login":"Akosmo","id":95504962,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbFKQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95504962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo","html_url":"https://github.com/Akosmo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T02:46:11Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T02:49:53Z","body":"> > Also, the sine sweep from the [#67650 (comment)](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/67650#issue-1415650951) is much better for explaining what an FFT does.\r\n> \r\n> What's the difference between the current demo and a sine sweep? (I'm not an audio specialist.)\r\n\r\nNot the person you asked, but the Fourier Transform formula takes signal from the time domain to the frequency domain. So basically taking audio samples/frames, and displaying which frequencies lead to those same samples, making the spectrum analyzer. A sweeping sine wave is better at displaying that behavior than a song with multiple instruments, like in the current demo project. It is better because you have a single sound and simple waveshape (sine waves only produce one frequency), with a clear pitch and behavior.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3708757274/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3713884029","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114355#issuecomment-3713884029","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114355","id":3713884029,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dXV99","user":{"login":"Akosmo","id":95504962,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbFKQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95504962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo","html_url":"https://github.com/Akosmo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-06T09:26:01Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T09:26:01Z","body":"Attempted to squash all commits, but couldn't squash the first one, because I was afraid of messing something up if I resetted too far back. Also rebased.\r\n\r\nI'm trying to get the text for the validation file, but no matter what I do, and despite getting help, the text won't show up. So just like the last time, I'll get the report from the automatic checks to use for the validation file, as expected. I'd keep the same one I had before, but I'm not sure if the errors are the same. Really sorry about that.\r\n\r\nI tried my best to keep the behavior related to `tap_back_pos` as close to original as possible. In order to do that, I created a variable in the compat include file. I did not use access modifiers, and I don't know how to test the file, since I've never worked with GDExtension.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3713884029/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3714041343","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114355#issuecomment-3714041343","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114355","id":3714041343,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dX8X_","user":{"login":"Akosmo","id":95504962,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbFKQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95504962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo","html_url":"https://github.com/Akosmo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/followers","following_url